SUMMARY:Scenic AVL - Hendersonville - with WNC American Pilgrims on the Ca
 mino
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the associat
 ion of American Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on th
 e WNC Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/A
 VLCamino/announcements).\n\nThis route starts with a five mile loop\, a co
 ffee break\, and a figure eight. We will stop at Southern Streams coffee t
 o chat about Camino preparation and the experience of walking the differen
 t routes\, including the Frances\, the Norte\, and the Portuguese. If you 
 are unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are a few links to learn more:\n\n*[
 American Pilgrims on the Camino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_direc
 tory/western-north-carolina/)\n- [Stingy Nomads Camino](https://stingynoma
 ds.com/camino-de-santiago-walking-guide/)\n*[Gronze Camino Planner](https:
 //www.gronze.com/)\n\n**Distance:** This hike is made up of three sections
 \, all crossing the Ecusta trail. You can join and hike as much or as litt
 le as you want 5 miles\, 7.5 or 10.5) For those who are just starting thei
 r training\, come out and do the first or second half!\n\n***9:30am **- Me
 et at First Congregational Church\, 1735 5th Ave W\, Hendersonville\, NC 2
 873\n*** First section is a five mile loop. **There is a short but steep c
 limb up to Davis Mountain Road\, with a short stretch along a gravel road.
  Pace will be 3.0 mph. The loop ends at Southern Streams coffee house\, wh
 ich is across from the church where we start.\n\n*** 11:00 am **- Southern
  Streams Coffee house\, near FCC church. 30 minute coffee break and camino
  chat. (if you want to sleep in\, meet us here at 11 ish)\n\n***Second Sec
 tion: **Starting at about 11:30 am from Southern Streams coffee\, continue
  through lower Laurel Park. For those who want to exit\, you can return to
  the church on the Ecusta Trail for a total of about 7 miles.\n\n*** Last 
 Section: **To downtown and St. James Church\, returning via Ecusta Trail. 
 10.5 miles total distance. We plan to arrive at the church around 1:15 pm.
 \n\n**Elevation Gain: **800 ft total if you do the full 10.5.\n**Pace: **3
 .0-3.2 mph\n**Surface: **Road\, with short stretch on gravel road.\n**Rati
 ng: **Strenuous for distance\, if you do the whole thing.\n**Features:**\n
 *Neighborhood charm\, last of the spring color\, Hendersonville downtown\,
  St James church.\n*No bears. There may be geese or ducks on Rhododendron 
 lake.\n\n**Cautions: **There are a few stretches on busy roads where we wi
 ll need to walk single file.\n\n**Full Route: **[Laurel Park Loop](https:/
 /www.alltrails.com/explore/map/laurel-park-loop-improved-3937230?u=i&sh=if
 wm3x)\n\n**Parking: **We are meeting at the First Congregational Church. P
 lease carpool if possible.\n\n**Gear: **2L water\, snacks\, cash for coffe
 e at Southern Streams.\n**Dogs: **On leash the entire time.\n**After Event
 : **Some of us will go to [ El Sol y La Luna\, ](https://maps.app.goo.gl/p
 fvgkMsJztNXAANi9)Cali-Mex\, after the hike.\n\n**Scenic Asheville Series: 
 **This hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on my Scenic Asheville Series.
  There are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1c
 NNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) in the series\; hike them al
 l and receive an [attractive badge](https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1go
 XUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for your backpack. Check y
 our status [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU
 5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\n\n**On-Time Departure**\nW
 e will start by walking the labyrinth at the First Congregational Church\,
  so this is a pretty relaxed start.\n\n- Please change your RSVP as soon a
 s you know you can't make it.\n*If you have questions\, call the hike lead
 er (Gracen) at 828-290-0886.\n\n**Guests:** For this hike\, there are no g
 uest restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release of Lia
 bility:**\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may have tra
 ffic and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Participants are responsible for t
 heir safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunte
 er and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to 
 organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknow
 ledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injurie
 s\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated
  with this event. You are responsible for any guests\, dogs or other compa
 nions you bring with you. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to 
 the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/te
 rms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314367727
 /
