SUMMARY:Cane Gap to the Blue Ridge Parkway Walkers Knob. Out/Back FITNESS 
 HIKE.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**It is an honor to be selected to
  lead this hike...thank you Allen for your confidence in me. I hope we don
 't end up in Tennessee\, or Oklahoma\, or something.**\n\n**Sign up begins
  6am on Sunday**\n\n**MEETUP OPTION:**\n**Carpool option:** Meet at **8:45
  am**\, at the I-26 Park and ride parking lot (exit 17) to follow or carpo
 ol. Pease post if you plan to meet us there\, otherwise see you at the TH 
 at 9:30 am. Trailhead is approximately 40-45 minutes from Weaverville.\n\n
 **HIKE DESCRIPTION\;**\nThis is a 12 mile 0&B back country STRENUOUS hike 
 along the ridgeline that opposes the Black Mountain Crest Trail\, passing 
 Little Butt and point misery and continues to the Walker's Knob on the Blu
 e Ridge Parkway for a snack break and return.\n\nThe trailhead begins at a
 n elevation of 4\,200 feet with an initial 1.5-mile climb with switchbacks
  to 5\,900' of elevation and then continues as a rollercoaster ridgeline t
 rek with beautiful mountain views. There are over 350 well-crafted wooden 
 steps ( out and back) on a trail which is mostly under a decidous forest. 
 The trail is maintained by the NC High Peaks Association. T**he elevation 
 gain estimates is approximately +/-3\,300 feet\, level 10\\*.** High Mount
 ain Temperatures on this hike are tipically 10+ degrees cooler than Ashevi
 lle.\n\n**PACE:** Fitness hikes proceed at a steady pace averaging 2.5 MPH
  on climbs and/or rugged trail conditions\, and 3+ MPH on level/downgrade 
 sections with brief regrouping at trail intersections\, or as needed. Ther
 e are plenty of cardiochallenges and endurance sections on this hike which
  is for conditioned hikers. Please know your hiking abilities before signi
 ng on. Any questions please post on this meetuo site or message me.\n\n**T
 railhead Directions**. Take the Barnardsville Hwy exit to **Rt. 197** off 
 I-26 and remain on this road to the trailhead. Several miles past Barnards
 ville **this road will transitions into a gravel forest road (also called 
 N. Fork Road). Continue to the mountaintop where the trailhead begins.** A
 t the mountain top\, the Forest Road will transition back to a paved road.
  You will see Ogle Meadows Rd (left) leading to a high mountain community 
 which is directly across from an old gated forest service road where the t
 railhead begins. Park alongside the old forest road. **If you reach the pa
 ved road at the mountain top you will have driven about 20 feet past the o
 ld forest road trailhead.**\n\nIf you sign up for this hike or waitlist an
 d change your mind go back to the RSVP link and cancel your reservation to
  free the space for other hikers.\n\n**Weather: Cancellation** and / resch
 eduling will be made on or before 7 AM hike day if inclimate weather forca
 sts indicates potential unsuitable conditions.\n\n**DOGS:** Trail-friendly
  dogs welcome\n\n**\\*HIKE LEVELS**...are based on the total elevation gai
 n (or estimates).\nLevel (1) Up to 600 feet of elevation gain.\nLevel (2) 
 600'- 900'\; Level (3) 900' - 1200'\; Level (4) 1200' - 1500'\; Level (5) 
 1\,500' - 1\,800'\; Level (6) 1\,800' - 2\,100'\; Level (7)\\* 2\,100' - 2
 \,400'\; Level (8) 2\,400' - 2700'\; Level (9) 2700' - 3000' **Level (10) 
 3000' - 4000'\;**\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe organizer of this trip
  is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organize
 r is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this eve
 nt you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all ris
 ks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, a
 nd associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agre
 e to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.c
 om/terms)\n\nULTIMATE HIKES are 4000+ feet elevation gain. I
